                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "My first run of Dyscourse was over in about an hour and I honestly thought that was it, but then I rewound a few days, sent different people on different tasks, and ended up with a completely different story. The paper craft art style and the soundtrack are easily the best parts, and the day rewind feature makes it painless to poke at every branch until the newspaper headline at the end finally shows everyone alive. The characters are loud stereotypes though, Teddy the conspiracy nut got on my nerves fast, and some consequences feel pulled out of nowhere, like someone dying from an egg I split a day earlier. If you enjoy choose your own adventure books and don't mind replaying the same dialogue to find new corners, it's worth it, but grab it on sale because full price stings for how short each run is.",
